#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""svc – the service gateway of tentaclAI: credentials, access modes (read/write/confirm) and audit for every tentacle.

One JSON file per service in $TC_DIR/services/*.json.
A service can have an "api", an "mcp" and/or a "git" part. Secrets are ${VAR} placeholders,
resolved from the stack's .env (read fresh on every call) and the container environment.

  svc list                         services, types, system, status (missing variables)
  svc systems [name]               systems (groups of services on one host) with SSH host, members and rules
  svc info <name> [--json]         description, URLs, docs, examples, notes (no secrets); --json: the service file as stored
  svc sync                         MCP -> Claude user config, clone missing git repos, regenerate /workspace/SERVICES.md
  svc <name> <METHOD> <path> [curl args...]
                                   API call with auth injected, e.g.
                                   svc arcane GET /environments
                                   svc mealie POST /households/shopping/items -d '{"note":"milk"}'
                                   HTTP 4xx/5xx exits non-zero (body printed) – unless -w reads the status
  svc git                          git repos: path, access (read/write), branch, ahead/behind, changes
  svc git sync [name...]           clone missing repos, apply settings, fetch
  svc git fetch|pull <name>        fetch from the remote (pull: also fast-forward the current branch)
  svc git push <name> [branch] [--force]   push a branch (credentials stay with svc)
  svc ssh <host> [command...]      command (or a shell) on an SSH host – per-host access, default confirm
  svc pending                      approvals waiting in tentacontrol → Approvals (and active grants)
  svc config put service <name> <file> | put system <name> <file> | put local <file> | put skill <name> <file>
                                   write a service file, a system file, the site rules (local/CLAUDE.md) or a site
                                   skill (local/skills/<name>/SKILL.md) – always needs approval; it shows the changes
  svc docker                       Docker hosts (via ssh, also this host): target, stacks dir, access
  svc docker <name> <args...>      docker CLI against that host, e.g. svc docker gate ps
  svc compose <name> <stack> <args...>
                                   docker compose in <stacks_dir>/<stack> of that host, e.g. svc compose gate pangolin ps
  (access "read": only read-only docker/compose commands are allowed)
  svc audit [n] [--since 24h] [search]   audit log: words, field:value, -field:value (actor user source type target action outcome)
  (access "confirm": writes wait for the user's approval in tentacontrol → Approvals)
  svc test <name>                  connection test of every part (api, mcp, git, docker, db, web, files)
  svc db [name] "<SQL>" | tables | describe <t> | shell    databases (postgres, mysql/mariadb); [--csv]
  svc web [name] [--links|--raw|--login] [path]          web sources: page as readable text, links, raw HTML
  svc mail [name|address] send|folders|list|read|flag|move … mail: send (smtp), read a mailbox (imap) – svc mail for details
  svc jobs [name] [--runs N] [--steps]                    scheduled jobs: list, a definition with its recent runs
  svc files [name] ls|tree|cat|grep|pull|diff|push [path] directories/files on SSH hosts (pull → /workspace/files/<name>)

Privilege separation: Claude runs as user "claude" and calls svc through sudo; svc runs as root (it alone can read
.env, the SSH keys and the service files) and starts client tools (curl, psql, mariadb, stdio MCP servers) as the
unprivileged user "tcrun" with only the secret they need. Anything run as root never touches Claude's files directly.

The code lives in /usr/local/lib/tentaclai/svclib (build/svclib in the repository) – see its __init__.py.
"""
import sys

sys.path.insert(0, "/usr/local/lib/tentaclai")
from svclib.cli import cli  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(cli(sys.argv, __doc__))
